The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
short lpa, bmcr;
get_registers(dev, BMCR, 2, &bmcr);
get_registers(dev, ANLP, 2, &lpa);
```
Reason:
The variables `lpa` and `bmcr` are declared but not initialized. If the `get_registers` function fails before assigning values to these variables, they will retain garbage values, leading to undefined behavior when used later in the function.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
short lpa = 0;
short bmcr = 0;
```
Reason:
By initializing `lpa` and `bmcr` to `0`, the code ensures that even if the `get_registers` function fails, these variables will have a defined value (zero) instead of garbage, preventing undefined behavior in subsequent operations.

